 "final_message": "Brightpath accepted Sam and Nadia's intent to proceed, and I've answered both underwriting conditions. Underwriting hasn't cleared the W-2 condition yet.\n\n- **Loan Estimate:** It was within all three limits. The rate is 7.25% (limit 7.5%), the total monthly payment is $3,485.58 (limit $3,600), and closing costs are $13,200 (limit $14,500). I recorded the intent to proceed, signed \"Sam Okafor-Reyes and Nadia Okafor-Reyes\".\n- **Documents:** I uploaded the 14 approved files, which are 8 bank statements (last 2 months for each of the four personal accounts), 4 payslips and 2 W-2s for tax year 2025. I then sent the package to underwriting. Nothing else was shared, and Nadia's Northgate business checking account stays out of it.\n- **Deposit condition:** The underwriter asked about the $8,000 deposit on 09/03/2026 into Sam's checking account. I asked Sam and Nadia, and they said it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, not a loan. I sent that explanation to Brightpath, and the condition now shows as \"responded\".\n- **W-2 condition:** I attached both 2025 W-2s directly to this condition. It still shows \"open\", so the underwriter needs to review them.\n\nThe next step is Brightpath's underwriting review. The application was submitted only once.",
